   "text": "Editor’s Note:\nAlbert Einstein was born in Ulm, Germany, in 1879. He was awarded the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1921. Driven into exile by Hitler’s advent to power, Professor Einstein came to this country in 1933, was appointed for life a member of the Institute for Advanced Study at Princeton, and became an American citizen in 1940.\nOn August 2, 1939, just a month before the outbreak of World War",
